 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<IntegerLinearProgramming\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e79a626-08be-43e4-80b6-bccf6b50550d"],
 " solve the exact integer program. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Exhaustive\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "557951a8-7ab1-4211-9119-5c0e0bce915b"],
 " remains a migration alias. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Greedy\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee833cd-f93f-43dd-86e6-67405f50fecf"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Symmetric\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "13128f05-5814-4eb2-9915-9f78e83c6d7d"],
 " are unsupported: the covering number is always the minimum. Obtain a \
greedy upper bound by taking the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["Length"]], "paclet:ref/Length"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
